Long story short, Firestone has a network issue that prevents ssh from =
working. This has been fixed by Tim here and the changes are in progress =
of being upstreamed:

=
https://github.com/madscientist159/openbmc-openbmc/commits/firestone-test-=
last-working =
<https://github.com/madscientist159/openbmc-openbmc/commits/firestone-test=
-last-working>

GIT hash 175c297c3e65e945ebb2df0cb4f4fcd2ba2e8779, branch =
firestone-test-last-working

You can build a firestone openbmc image from that repository to get =
network working.


